For my latest project I wanted to see if I could get the "Truest
Pacifist (who was actually a genocidal maniac and not really a
pacifist)", or "Fewest Kills" or whatever is decided on.  At first I
was basing my effort on having fewer than ekiM's 412 vanquished kills
but in a previous attempt I suffered some genocidal confusion and came
in at 414 kills.  It turns out that genociding a type of creature
"kills" any existing creatures in existence ... oops.  So I gave it
another try and part way in I decided to add another Stupid Ascension
Trick (tm) and not kill any unique monsters and made it to 257 kills
and no Unique's.  This YAAP is kind of long but if I left anything out
please feel free to ask.  Thanks again HJC for your discussion of life
as a foocubus; it seemed to me silly at the time but was perfect for
this situation.

Interestingly enough, my wizard's starting spell was rather
underwhelming:
Wizard lock ... meh, which was a bit of a disappointment after losing
two YASD's where I started with sleep and identify.  I did not find
any bones files.

Unfortunately I tend to have so many deaths that I forget the details
of the early game, but here's the general overview:
Started out by stranding my starting pet on the first level and coming
back up just to pet-test for cursed-ness and to credit clone from
shops.  To keep my kill list low I kept my pet out of fights and
tried to only kill monsters if they got significantly in my way and
dust engraved Elbereth early and often.  In Sokoban I lucked out and
got a Bag of Holding, yay!

I killed monsters until about XL 5 or 1000 xp and then I found 2
adjacent sink levels and danced with some lovely demons until level 15
or 16 or something.   I ran down to Minetown trying not to be in line
with the gnomes and dwarves killing each other to get to me.  Minetown
was cross-aligned so I didn't hang around much and just headed down to
get the luckstone.

Before going on the quest I sacrificed for MagicBane on a co-aligned
level 10 altar and engraved Elbereth to avoid most fights.  It's
amazing how many monsters respect Elbereth!  Also prior to going on
the quest I rubbed a magic lamp for a magic marker and wrote some
genocide scrolls (it took 2 tries).  First was ; so that I wouldn't
tally the quest eels and gremlins were removed prior to finding any
big sources of water.  L were genocided prior to any annoying
summoning storms or guaranteed appearances.

I was going to genocide 'y', 'e' to avoid the kamikaze monsters but by
the time I had the scrolls I had already avoided several and figured
that I could try to avoid killing e's and y's and have fewer than if I
killed all of the ones still lurking around.  Correct, I think.
Ravens were almost genocided because they are annoying and mess up my
Elbereth engraving (Umber Hulks, too.) but I didn't have enough magic
marker charges and just toughed it out.

Following my previous ascension I decided to play as an incubus to
steal the Quest artifacts.  I also realized that without killing
monsters (especially high level ones) there is significantly less loot
to be had so I turned to a life of theft and petty crime.  With my
rings of polymorph and polymorph control I turned into an incubus and
stole the Quest artifacts from the Dark One, Vlad, and Rodney.  In one
potential setback, Rodney stole the Amulet of Yendor back from me.
So, I hit him with a potion of paralysis and fled.  Then I had to don
my rings and wait until I could re-polymorph, re-wield a !oPara and re-
steal the amulet.

Asmodeus and Baalzebub were both paid off and Orcus had his wand
stolen and then assisted me with recovering the amulet.  Fortunately,
Orcus was polite enough to wait while I re-polymorphed into an incubus
and stole the amulet from him (thanks to Elbereth).  Monster summoning
was handled by a combination of Elbereth and polymorph spell.

The residents of the Castle fared very well and suffered 0 casualties
as I crept in over the battlements, into the corner tower and
recovered the Wand of Wishing (0:3, yay!).  With the wand I wished for
a magic marker and wrote a spellbook of polymorph, and then found out
that I couldn't cast it because I was unskilled. So I wrote a
spellbook of knock, spammed it, and got polymorph down to 0% failure.
the RNG was extremely benign and my collected wands were poly'ed into
teleportation rather easily.

I had recovered most of the loose loot in the dungeon and thus began
my theft of most of Gehennom's residents' possessions.  This behavior
left me somewhat exposed as I wore only +5 dexterity gloves, +5
(starting) cloak of magic resistance, and an iron helm.  An incubus
only has 20-30 hp but even still I was able to live through hits from
minotaurs and the Wizard of Yendor.  I would zap detect treasure, put
on a blindfold, and then Call the monsters that appeared to be
carrying scrolls and potions.  The collected potions and wands were
polymorphed and the wands of digging stolen from minotaurs were
polymorphed into /oTeleportation.

On the ascension run I had a stockpile of paralysis potions (9 of
them) that allowed me to elude Rodney.  Trouble was the "mysterious
force" kicked in right after I passed him by and I had to keep re-
paralyzing him.  I also used up my wand of digging at the same time
because of Juiblex.  The other trouble was (just remembered) I left a
stash on Level 20 with my spare potions of paralysis and thus ran out
while in Gehennom so I used 2 wishes for potions of paralysis.

