I had a strange happening on the Plane of Earth.  I wanted to avoid
encountering the Wizard at the beginning of the Plane of Earth so I
sat on an Elbereth on DLVL 1 until he showed up.  In the meantime I
tried to keep monsters alive by polymorphing the spitters, umber
hulks, and humans.  In retrospect I should have waited somewhere other
than in a room to avoid the "collateral damage" casualties due to
dragons, hellhounds and iron golems.  Anyhow, eventually he showed up
so I hit him with a potion of paralysis, grabbed the amulet and
climbed.  Now, here is the weird part, upon arrival on the Plane of
Earth I got the "...elude me, fool" message which I was not expecting
but in the cavern was the minotaur, the elvenking, and a yellow c,
yeah, a cockatrice.  Being out of wands of digging I killed the
minotaur, grabbed his wand of digging (elf was peaceful) and hit the
cockatrice with a potion of paralysis.  Then I got "wait, that is the
Wizard of Yendor" or something like that and my attack did not
process, kind of like when you get a "wait there's something there"
message, but he turned into a purple @.  On my next strike with the
potion, the potion crashed, he froze and I made for the portal.
Unlike a previous experience the Wizard did not follow me through the
portal to Air.  Anyone ever sen this happen?

The Plane of Air used 15 or so teleport zaps and 5 or so polymorphs.
I think I avoided killing any of the air elementals that engulfed me
("You break out of the horse's stomach!") but none of the vortexes
died.

Fire was easy and water was easy once I put on my ring of conflict.
The portal to the Astral Plane found me so I was confronted by
hostility on the Astral Plane, which was good because I didn't want my
guardian angel killing things.  I made for the left altar since it was
famine hoping to teleport and jump my way past.  I did not have my
create monster scrolls sufficiently prepped but I was hoping to create
acid blobs to immobilize the Riders but after my leg got better from a
xan attack I jumped my way to the Lawful altar ... hehe.  So I wished
for a helm of opposite alignment, dropped all of my artifacts,
amulets, and gems (to keep a low score) and offered the amulet!

